{
  "id": 120344643,
  "iid": 4519,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "dfilter: Fix parsing of octal character escape sequences",
  "description": "Octal escape sequences \\NNN can have between 1 and 3 digits. If\nthe sequence had less than 3 digits the parser got out of sync\nwith an incorrect double increment of the pointer and errors out\nparsing sequences like \\0, \\2 or \\33.\n\nBefore:\n  Filter: ip.proto == '\\33'\n  dftest: \"'\\33'\" is too long to be a valid character constant.\n\nAfter:\n  Filter: ip.proto == '\\33'\n\n  Constants:\n  00000 PUT_FVALUE\t27 <FT_UINT8> -> reg#1\n\n  Instructions:\n  00000 READ_TREE\t\tip.proto -> reg#0\n  00001 IF-FALSE-GOTO\t3\n  00002 ANY_EQ\t\treg#0 == reg#1\n  00003 RETURN\n\nFixes #16525.",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2021-10-07T18:15:22.230Z",
